  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find centers (1 or 2) and markers (3 or 7)\n    centers = []  # (r, c, type)\n    markers = []  # (r, c, type)\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val == 1:\n                centers.append((r, c, 1))\n            elif val == 2:\n                centers.append((r, c, 2))\n            elif val == 3:\n                markers.append((r, c, 3))\n            elif val == 7:\n                markers.append((r, c, 7))\n    \n    # Initialize output grid with zeros\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Place centers in output\n    for r, c, t in centers:\n        out[r][c] = t\n    \n    # For each center, find markers of the corresponding type in same row or column\n    for r, c, t in centers:\n        if t == 1:\n            target_marker = 7\n        elif t == 2:\n            target_marker = 3\n        else:\n            continue\n            \n        for mr, mc, mt in markers:\n            if mt != target_marker:\n                continue\n            \n            # Check if in same row\n            if mr == r and mc != c:\n                if mc < c:  # West\n                    nr, nc = r, c - 1\n                else:  # East\n                    nr, nc = r, c + 1\n                if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                    out[nr][nc] = target_marker\n            # Check if in same column\n            elif mc == c and mr != r:\n                if mr < r:  # North\n                    nr, nc = r - 1, c\n                else:  # South\n                    nr, nc = r + 1, c\n                if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                    out[nr][nc] = target_marker\n    \n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    \n    # Find centers (1 or 2) and markers (3 or 7)\n    centers = []  # (r, c, type)\n    markers = []  # (r, c, type)\n    \n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val == 1:\n                centers.append((r, c, 1))\n            elif val == 2:\n                centers.append((r, c, 2))\n            elif val == 3:\n                markers.append((r, c, 3))\n            elif val == 7:\n                markers.append((r, c, 7))\n    \n    # Initialize output grid with zeros\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]\n    \n    # Place centers in output\n    for r, c, t in centers:\n        out[r][c] = t\n    \n    # For each center, find markers of the corresponding type in same row or column\n    for r, c, t in centers:\n        if t == 1:\n            target_marker = 7\n        elif t == 2:\n            target_marker = 3\n        else:\n            continue\n            \n        for mr, mc, mt in markers:\n            if mt != target_marker:\n                continue\n            \n            # Check if in same row\n            if mr == r and mc != c:\n                if mc < c:  # West\n                    nr, nc = r, c - 1\n                else:  # East\n                    nr, nc = r, c + 1\n                if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                    out[nr][nc] = target_marker\n            # Check if in same column\n            elif mc == c and mr != r:\n                if mr < r:  # North\n                    nr, nc = r - 1, c\n                else:  # South\n                    nr, nc = r + 1, c\n                if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                    out[nr][nc] = target_marker\n    \n    return out",
